## Prerequisites

- Python **3.13**
- [uv](https://github.com/astral-sh/uv)
- Docker (Postgres via Compose)

## Quick start

```bash
uv sync
make test    # Postgres in Docker + agent on host (uv run agent)
```

Or run the full stack in Docker:

```bash
make run
```

See `make help` for all commands (`db`, `test`, `run`, `down`).

## Configuration

- **`agent.yml`** — agent identity, protocols, rate limits, runtime settings
- **`.env`** — secrets (Postgres, Agentverse API key, payment provider keys)
- **`.env.example`** — reference for available env vars

## Project layout

```
{{ project_name }}/
├── agent.yml           # Non-secret configuration
├── .env                # Secrets (never commit)
├── .env.example        # Env var reference
├── AGENTVERSE.md       # Agentverse profile readme (published on register)
├── schema.sql          # Postgres coordination schema
├── docker-compose.yml  # Local Postgres + agent
├── Makefile            # db, test, run, down
├── src/agent/handler.py  # Your handler (edit this)
├── src/runtime/        # Framework runtime (do not edit unless extending)
└── src/shared/         # Settings and shared types
```

## Agentverse

Set `AGENTVERSE_API_KEY` in `.env` to register automatically on startup. Edit `AGENTVERSE.md` for your Agentverse profile page.

